### T3: the differential in the ladder's sieve regime
### added: 2026-09-16T18:21:05Z
###
### T1 and T2 above could not reach the regime where the timing
### difference appears: their small_high is 3,163 and 10,001, so the sieve
### rescans only a few hundred base primes per tile. T3 uses a high limit
### with a low --p-small, giving the full-size base-prime list and frequent
### Phase 1 failure at once.
###
### cmd: ./bin/goldbach 1000040000000 --start=1000000000000 \
###          --seg-size=200000000 --p-small=1000 --batch-size=2000000
###
### 2x10^7 even numbers near 10^12. Confirmed from the run:
###   small_high     = 1000021  ("Building small primes bitset up to 1000021")
###   base primes    = 78,499 rescanned per tile (the ladder rescans 78,498)
###   candidates     = 168 primes <= 1000
###
### Three runs per build.

